@startuml
!include ../themes/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/starchess-achievements.puml
' purpose: StarChess trophy gallery + a new-unlock gate before rematch
' status: type + catalog defined 2026-09-22; evaluators and UI not built
' covers: apps/starchess/src/screens/ReviewScreen.tsx
'         apps/starchess/src/screens/SingleScreen.tsx
'         apps/starchess/src/store/matchHistoryStore.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/achievements/catalog.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/achievements/evaluate.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/store/achievementStore.ts
'         apps/starchess/src/components/features/AchievementsModal.tsx
' live spec to update when this ships:
'         _spec/apps/starchess/menu-flow.puml
'         (today: gameOver opens MatchResultModal directly)
' difficulty plan this branch also honors, and does not reopen:
'         _spec/_plans/chess-save-difficulty.puml
'         OUTDATED — Coach elo already restores. Achievements key off
'         StarChessGameRecord.opponent (naive|strategic), never a second
'         difficulty enum and never chess_coach_settings_state.
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' Two surfaces, one catalog.
'   1. Review list: a third button in ArenaLibrary's .arenaFileRow,
'      after "Choose arena JSON" and "Export history JSON".
'      Label: Achievements. It opens the gallery modal.
'   2. /single gameOver: after addMatchRecord, if this game is the
'      witness for any newly filled id, show that modal first.
'      Continue then opens MatchResultModal (Another Game / Replay).
'      Zero new ids skips straight to MatchResultModal.
'
' The gallery is 12 cards, one per shortId. Desktop lays them
' three across, using the desktop width. An obtained card reads
' "Obtained (Level N)" and fills N of 5 bars. Its glyph uses that
' level's material. A missing card is dimmed, bars empty, and is
' not a link. Not a piece under public/pieces.
'
' Clicking an obtained card navigates to /review/:id for the witness
' game and closes the modal. A higher level replaces the lower id.
' The card shows that highest level, not a row per level.
'
' One AchievementsModal. Gallery mode: 12 cards, NeonModal close.
' On desktop the sheet is min(56rem, calc(100vw - 4rem)). Do not
' widen .panel--md / .panel--lg. Fresh mode: only the new cards,
' dismissible false, no overlay close, one Continue button
' (variant neon). Fresh title: New achievements.
'
' ── TYPE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Achievement.id = "<level>-<type>-<shortId>"
'   level 1..5, type scfen | count | analysis, shortId has no hyphen.
'   title max 25, description max 75, icon is that svg file's URL.
' Materials: 1 wood, 2 Silver, 3 Gold, 4 BTC, 5 Anti-matter.
' Source of the rows: apps/starchess/src/achievements/catalog.ts
'
' Every description names its level. Adjutant-scaled families name who
' was beaten: "Beat the Naive Adjutant" … "Beat the RLCD Adjutant"
' (Naive, Strategic, ML, RLHF, RLCD). Score families state the
' threshold: "Promote 3 Marines in a game".
' A win vs Strategic grants level 2 instead of level 1. A harder
' tier levels the same shortId up, through RLCD at level 5.
' Wins at a tier or harder count toward that level's threshold.
' SHIPPED: the win tally is every game ever recorded — the union of
' match-history wins and the won ids kept in starchess_achievement_career
' (careerWins in achievementLive.ts). The kept ids outlive the 150-game
' history window; the old per-tier counters are a floor, never added on top.
' SHIPPED: in-game (analysis/scfen score) levels announced mid-match are
' granted with the match record at game end, win, loss or draw
' (finalizeAchievementLive returns them). Leaving mid-match grants nothing.
'
'   shortId   title                 type      levels
'   beat      Human Training        count     1 win, easy, adjutant tier
'   beat50   Human Training        count     50 wins, easy
'   flawless  Flawless Training     scfen     1 flawless win, hard, tier
'   cheese    Cheese Master         scfen     20/16/13/11/9 turns, easy
'   stonks    Stonks                analysis  3/6/10/15/20, easy
'   Stonks nets one piece: captured UNIT_COST, starting at minus that
'   piece's own cost. The cost is the birth type on turn-type-origin.
'   A queen trade nets 0. A pawn (1) that takes a queen (9) nets 8.
'   gogo      GO GO GO!             analysis  1/2/3/5/7 promotions, hard
'   medal     Medal of Honor        analysis  marine dies intercepting, 1/3/5/7/10, impossible
'   vision    Ready to roll out!    scfen     2/4/7/10/15 full-vision, hard
'   mines     Is that it?           analysis  1/2/4/7/10 mine hits, hard
'   mecha     Target Designated     analysis  1/2/3/5/7, impossible
'   juke      Make it happen        scfen     2/4/7/10/15 jumps, hard
'   light     Let there be Light    scfen     3/7/10/14/20 defensive captures, hard
' Medal of Honor and Ready to roll out! were both numbered 8.
' Dropping the 10-win Human Training card leaves 12.
'
' ── EVALUATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Pure read of stored records. Never call endScTurn or scOutcome.
' count reads win tallies. scfen and analysis read saved snapshots
' and resolves. They do not replay the rules engine.
'
' A live record has no arenaPlayers. Tutorials never write history.
' Arena imports and file imports do not open the end modal. They also
' do not satisfy predicates. Re-imported live games (no arenaPlayers)
' can fill a still-empty slot on the next backfill. History export
' JSON gains no field.
'
' Witness order: live records by endedAt ascending, then id ascending.
' The first record that reaches a level owns that level.
' A higher level replaces the lower id for the same shortId.
' unlockedAt is that record's endedAt.
' A missing opponent matches no Adjutant tier.
' Leave-without-a-record still unlocks nothing. If forfeit-as-loss
' later writes a live loss, that record is eligible like any other.
'
' Store key starchess_achievements, via createPersistedStore:
'   { unlocks: { [id]: { gameId, unlockedAt } } }
' achievementStore does not import matchHistoryStore.
' It publishes pinnedGameIds() at init. addMatchRecord reads that
' set: non-witness games still cap at MAX_GAMES (150); a witness id
' is kept even when it falls outside that window. One copy of each id.
'
' End-of-game order inside SingleScreen, after the record is saved:
'   before = unlock ids
'   backfill(matchHistory())     ' oldest witness fills empty slots
'   fresh = ids added whose gameId is this match
'   fresh.length > 0 → New achievements modal, else result modal
' Continue sets the fresh modal closed and the result modal open.
' Another Game / Replay stay on MatchResultModal; this plan does
' not add a third button there.
' backfill also runs when the Review list mounts, so the gallery
' reflects games already in history without popping the end modal.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   Coach achievements or settingsStore.difficulty
'   the evaluator bodies (catalog names each measure)
'   putting achievements in the history export file
'   tutorial clears as achievements
'   analytics charts (chess-analytics.puml)
title PLANNED — trophies from saved games;\nnew ones precede rematch

component "ReviewScreen\nAchievements button" as BTN <<app>>
component "AchievementsModal\ngallery" as GAL <<app>>
component "catalog + backfill" as EVAL <<app>>
database "starchess_achievements" as UNLOCK <<db>>
database "starchess_match_history" as HIST <<db>>
component "SingleScreen\nafter addMatchRecord" as END <<app>>
component "New achievements\nfresh ids only" as NEW <<app>>
component "MatchResultModal\nAnother Game · Replay" as RESULT <<app>>
component "**re-resolve the match**" as RESCORE <<error>>
component "**arena or tutorial\ncounts as a win**" as ARENA <<error>>

BTN ARROW_MAIN GAL : open
GAL ARROW_MAIN EVAL : read catalog
EVAL ARROW_MAIN UNLOCK : first witness
EVAL ARROW_OPTIONAL HIST : live records
END ARROW_MAIN EVAL : backfill then diff
EVAL ARROW_MAIN NEW : this game witnessed
NEW ARROW_MAIN RESULT : Continue
EVAL ARROW_OPTIONAL RESULT : no new id
GAL ARROW_MAIN HIST : opens ""/review/:id""
EVAL ARROW_ERROR RESCORE
EVAL ARROW_ERROR ARENA

note right of BTN
  **Third control in the arena row,
  after Export history JSON.**
  The label is Achievements. It
  opens the gallery only.
end note

note bottom of GAL
  **Twelve cards, three across
  on desktop.** Obtained reads
  "Obtained (Level N)" and fills
  N of 5 bars. Missing stays dim
  and does not open a game.
end note

note bottom of NEW
  **Open only when this save is
  the witness for a new id.**
  Continue then shows Another
  Game and Replay. No new id
  skips this modal.
end note

note bottom of RESCORE
  **Read the saved record, never
  ""endScTurn"".** ""count"" levels
  by Adjutant tier. Other levels
  are one game's measure. A blank
  opponent matches no tier.
end note

note bottom of ARENA
  **A record with ""arenaPlayers""
  is not a live game.** Tutorials
  never write history. The fresh
  modal runs only on ""/single"".
end note

note right of HIST
  **A higher level replaces the
  lower id for that shortId.**
  The witness is the game that
  reached the current level.
  Trim still keeps that game.
end note

legend bottom
  **Order**
  ==
  **1. Type and catalog.** Families
  live in ""achievements/catalog.ts"".
  Tests pin ids, limits, ladders.
  --
  **2. Review button and gallery.**
  Unlocked card → ""/review/:id"".
  ==
  **3. End gate on /single.** Backfill,
  then the fresh modal, then the
  existing result modal.
  --
  **Also on this branch:** leave
  ""chess-save-difficulty.puml"" closed.
  No Coach elo key, no export field.
end legend
@enduml
